WEBVTT

00:03.520 --> 00:05.181
Would you like the last sausage?

00:05.355 --> 00:06.447
How about we split it?

00:06.623 --> 00:07.749
Okay.

00:07.924 --> 00:09.824
Meet you in the middle.

00:11.094 --> 00:13.654
Oh, ha, ha. Okay. Sexy.

00:20.770 --> 00:21.964
CHARLIE:
Aw!

00:22.138 --> 00:24.333
Nothing says love
like a little morning pork.

00:27.110 --> 00:30.807
Oh, hey. You're home early.
How was Vegas?

00:32.182 --> 00:34.514
- Never again.
- Oh, you lost?

00:34.684 --> 00:38.677
No, Alan, I won so much freaking money
that I'm embarrassed to go back.

00:41.191 --> 00:44.456
All right.
Well, uh, you remember Melissa?

00:44.627 --> 00:46.117
Of course, he remembers me.

00:46.296 --> 00:48.628
He deflowered me then dumped me.

00:50.433 --> 00:53.698
No offense, sweetheart, but your flower
had been plucked and potted...

00:53.870 --> 00:55.633
...long before I met you.

00:56.039 --> 00:58.974
Okay, okay, okay. Look, look.
Ha, ha. We're all adults here.

00:59.142 --> 01:01.474
Ha, ha. This doesn't have to be awkward.

01:01.644 --> 01:06.081
I mean, sure, Melissa is my receptionist
and sure, she was with you...

01:06.249 --> 01:08.809
...and sure, that ended badly,
but uh-

01:12.655 --> 01:15.123
Okay, I guess this does
have to be awkward.

01:15.391 --> 01:18.417
- Shouldn't we be getting ready for work?
- Yes, yes, let's do that.

01:18.595 --> 01:20.256
- You wanna shower together?
- Oh, great.

01:20.430 --> 01:22.421
Uh, let me just, uh,
start without you.

01:22.599 --> 01:24.999
There's a couple of things
I'd like to pre-wash.

01:26.202 --> 01:28.966
There's a mental image I didn't need.

01:29.706 --> 01:31.173
Charlie, I need to talk to you.

01:32.175 --> 01:35.110
I'm sorry I was a jerk.
I'm happy for you and Alan.

01:35.278 --> 01:39.271
I will kick myself for the rest of my life
for losing someone as special as you.

01:39.783 --> 01:41.683
No, silly, it's about something else.

01:41.851 --> 01:44.513
Oh, good, because even I
didn't believe that.

01:46.055 --> 01:48.615
Alan's birthday is next Saturday.

01:49.392 --> 01:51.360
Really? I don't think so.

01:51.728 --> 01:53.389
Yeppers, he's gonna be 40.

01:53.863 --> 01:57.924
Wow, that is so weird.
My baby brother's gonna be 40.

01:58.468 --> 02:00.629
- How old are you?
- Thirty-nine.

02:02.605 --> 02:04.630
That's what makes it so weird.

02:05.375 --> 02:08.742
Anyway, I think we should have a party
for him.

02:09.312 --> 02:10.870
Why?

02:11.047 --> 02:12.981
Because it's an important birthday...

02:13.149 --> 02:16.778
...and he deserves a big party
with all his friends and loved ones.

02:16.953 --> 02:19.979
All right, all right. Let's break this down.

02:20.156 --> 02:23.250
You want him to get what he deserves,
with his friends and loved ones...

02:23.426 --> 02:24.723
- ...and you want it big.
- Uh-huh.

02:24.894 --> 02:26.759
Pick one.

02:27.263 --> 02:29.128
Come on, Charlie,
don't be such a pooper.

02:29.299 --> 02:31.665
If it's gonna be a fun party,
I- I need your help.

02:32.001 --> 02:34.561
You want it to be fun?
Don't invite Alan.

02:34.737 --> 02:36.204
- Charlie-
- Okay, okay.

02:36.372 --> 02:39.307
You know who would love to help you
out with this? Our mom.

02:39.475 --> 02:40.908
- Really?
- Oh, yeah.

02:41.077 --> 02:44.274
Nothing she likes better
than extending herself for other people.

02:45.448 --> 02:48.008
- Good idea. I'll give her a call.
- You do that.

02:49.519 --> 02:52.420
Wait till she hears Alan's 40.

03:27.190 --> 03:30.853
Charlie, wake up.
I need to talk to you.

03:31.027 --> 03:34.019
&lt;i>CHARLIE:
Don't move, don't blink.&lt;/i>

03:34.764 --> 03:36.664
&lt;i>Maybe she'll think you're dead and leave.&lt;/i>

03:37.033 --> 03:38.500
I know you can hear me, Charlie.

03:38.668 --> 03:40.533
&lt;i>CHARLIE:
She's bluffing.&lt;/i>

03:41.337 --> 03:42.531
&lt;i>Just stay still.&lt;/i>

03:46.142 --> 03:47.609
&lt;i>Okay, don't panic.&lt;/i>

03:47.777 --> 03:51.508
&lt;i>You've experienced oxygen deprivation
before.&lt;/i>

03:51.681 --> 03:53.046
CHARLIE:
I can't breathe, Mom.

03:54.317 --> 03:55.614
Oh, good, you're awake.

03:57.820 --> 03:59.185
What can I do for you?

03:59.355 --> 04:02.916
I received a very unsettling message
on my answering machine...

04:03.092 --> 04:05.788
...and I would like you
to explain it to me.

04:05.962 --> 04:10.695
Okay, look, sometimes the liquor
makes me say hateful things.

04:10.867 --> 04:14.496
No, this message was from some woman
named Melissa.

04:14.671 --> 04:16.468
Oh, Alan's receptionist.

04:17.307 --> 04:19.104
Really? From the sound of her voice...

04:19.275 --> 04:22.472
...I'd guess she earns her living
baking cookies in a hollow tree.

04:24.414 --> 04:29.511
Anyway, she's somehow gotten it into her
head that Alan is turning 40 on Saturday.

04:29.686 --> 04:30.914
Yeah, so?

04:31.087 --> 04:32.349
Is she insane?

04:32.522 --> 04:35.252
Running around telling people
my son is 40.

04:35.725 --> 04:37.955
I know. She's a bad person.

04:39.896 --> 04:43.662
And that's not all.
She wants me to help with a party.

04:44.167 --> 04:48.729
Where in God's name
could she have gotten such an idea?

04:49.906 --> 04:51.806
Beats me.

04:52.642 --> 04:55.941
Maybe the fact that you're his mother
confused the poor girl.

05:03.619 --> 05:05.052
Oh, you're up.

05:05.221 --> 05:08.190
You've been cleaning in there
this whole time?

05:08.358 --> 05:11.122
Sure, let's say I was cleaning.

05:11.561 --> 05:14.359
If you're going out,
can I pull your car out of the garage?

05:14.530 --> 05:16.862
I don't want you pulling my car
out of the garage.

05:17.033 --> 05:20.400
Okay, I won't. From now on.

05:21.871 --> 05:23.805
Hey, what's, uh-?
What's going on up here?

05:24.240 --> 05:25.537
Ugh, terrific.

05:25.842 --> 05:29.471
This meeting of the worst club in history
can now come to order.

05:29.645 --> 05:32.273
Madam President, you have the floor.

05:32.849 --> 05:35.579
Oh, I get it. Heh. Sorry to interrupt.

05:35.752 --> 05:38.346
Go back to what you were planning,
uh, uh- Doing, uh. Whatever.

05:40.356 --> 05:45.384
Oh, uh, apropos of nothing, uh,
I like red velvet cake and close-up magic.

05:48.364 --> 05:49.888
Crap.

05:50.066 --> 05:51.624
Now we have to throw him a party.

05:52.201 --> 05:54.260
- Who?
- Your father.

05:54.604 --> 05:57.232
- Why?
- It's his birthday.

05:57.407 --> 05:58.669
Oh.

05:58.841 --> 06:00.069
Can I bring a date?

06:01.377 --> 06:03.436
- You got a date?
- That depends.

06:03.613 --> 06:06.582
- On what?
- Can I borrow your car?

06:07.683 --> 06:09.116
You don't got a date.

06:12.588 --> 06:14.579
We don't, uh-
We don't have to go out to dinner...

06:14.757 --> 06:16.384
...just because it's my birthday.

06:16.559 --> 06:19.392
Don't be silly.
This is a very special night.

06:19.562 --> 06:21.257
How many times do you turn 40?

06:21.431 --> 06:23.626
In my family, three or four.

06:24.333 --> 06:26.631
Well, the first time
is the one that counts.

06:27.703 --> 06:30.763
Okay. So- So it's just us, right?

06:31.607 --> 06:34.303
Of course it's just us.
Who else would it be?

06:34.477 --> 06:38.072
I don't know. My friends, family.

06:38.247 --> 06:39.976
A close-up magician.

06:41.484 --> 06:43.679
Oh, darn. What gave it away?

06:43.853 --> 06:47.084
When I left, Jake was taking a shower,
Charlie had on long pants...

06:47.256 --> 06:50.419
...and Berta said she was going
to some loser's birthday party.

06:52.028 --> 06:54.622
Oh, good, I had her down as a maybe.

06:55.064 --> 06:56.497
Promise you'll act surprised.

07:00.570 --> 07:04.165
Oh- Ha, ha. Oh, my God,
what a surprise!

07:10.179 --> 07:11.646
I don't know these people.

07:12.715 --> 07:14.148
We have a private room.

07:15.985 --> 07:17.043
Sorry, sorry.

07:18.621 --> 07:20.555
We've got a private room.

07:21.157 --> 07:22.590
Go back to your dinner. Heh.

07:22.758 --> 07:24.589
Ooh, Gazpacho.

07:27.430 --> 07:28.556
This is so nice.

07:28.731 --> 07:31.029
A private, intimate dinner
for just the two of us.

07:31.200 --> 07:34.533
Oh, my God, you guys.

07:39.709 --> 07:41.108
There's nobody here.

07:41.277 --> 07:43.575
I don't understand it.
I told them to be here an hour ago.

07:44.947 --> 07:46.278
Yeah, well, what are you gonna do?

07:46.449 --> 07:50.510
My family are a bunch of thoughtless,
selfish butt wipes.

07:53.189 --> 07:55.214
Surprise.

08:01.030 --> 08:02.088
Evelyn, smile.

08:02.265 --> 08:03.289
Uh!

08:04.400 --> 08:05.492
Oh, that's a keeper.

08:05.668 --> 08:09.069
Oh, uh- Listen, are you gonna be
cutting the cake soon?

08:09.238 --> 08:11.968
Because, actually,
I have a real party to go to.

08:12.141 --> 08:14.336
You can't go.
We haven't done the speeches yet.

08:14.510 --> 08:15.534
Oh, of course.

08:17.580 --> 08:19.309
Were we supposed to write speeches?

08:19.715 --> 08:21.740
- For what?
- For Alan.

08:22.385 --> 08:24.615
Let him write his own speech.

08:25.988 --> 08:27.979
Uh, can I have
your attention please? Ha, ha.

08:28.157 --> 08:31.718
I wanna thank you all for coming
to celebrate this wonderful occasion.

08:31.894 --> 08:33.384
I thought it was Alan's birthday.

08:36.666 --> 08:40.067
Now it's time to say a few words
about the guest of honor.

08:40.336 --> 08:41.860
I can think of a few words.

08:43.573 --> 08:47.703
Not only is he a terrific doctor
and fantastic boss...

08:48.044 --> 08:53.846
...he is also good and kind
and smart and funny...

08:54.016 --> 08:56.109
...and a really swell kisser.

08:56.285 --> 08:58.253
I can still hear you.

08:58.421 --> 09:03.552
Sorry I'm late. I was burning a fatty
with one of the busboys in the parking lot.

09:03.726 --> 09:05.057
How are you?

09:06.295 --> 09:10.095
Everyone, this is my mother, Shelly.
Mom, this is Alan's mother, Evelyn, and-

09:10.266 --> 09:14.669
Sweetie, save your breath, because I'm way
too toasted to remember a lot of names.

09:16.172 --> 09:18.504
Ooh, bread.

09:23.846 --> 09:27.043
All right, well, uh, now that we're
all here, why don't we take turns...

09:27.216 --> 09:30.743
...saying something about Alan
and how much he means to us.

09:32.121 --> 09:33.952
Okay, Jake, you wanna start?

09:34.123 --> 09:35.920
No, I gotta go make room for cake.

09:36.993 --> 09:41.089
All right. Uh-
Berta, why don't you get the ball rolling?

09:41.998 --> 09:44.091
Sure, what the hell.

09:46.302 --> 09:51.262
Zippy, I gotta tell you, when you
first moved in, I didn't really care for you.

09:52.775 --> 09:56.267
You were a persnickety, self-righteous,
smug son of a bitch.

09:57.580 --> 10:00.140
And now here we are, six years later.

10:02.051 --> 10:03.609
Thank you.

10:06.789 --> 10:08.552
Hear, hear.

10:08.991 --> 10:11.016
Oh, okay, anyone else?

10:11.193 --> 10:13.661
Okay. I'll go.

10:16.632 --> 10:20.966
I have pictures of myself
dressed in a forest ranger's uniform...

10:21.137 --> 10:26.302
...and I have absolutely no memory
of ever working as a forest ranger.

10:26.575 --> 10:27.940
Thank you.

10:32.048 --> 10:33.777
Alrighty.

10:34.717 --> 10:37.515
Uh, who's next? Evelyn?

10:38.087 --> 10:41.215
Me? Isn't it enough I carried him
for seven and a half months?

10:41.390 --> 10:44.382
You'd be surprised how many women
opt for the full nine.

10:45.494 --> 10:49.590
- Come on, you have to say something.
- Oh, fine.

10:50.199 --> 10:52.167
Alan, darling...

10:52.335 --> 10:54.303
...you were always the good son.

10:55.805 --> 10:59.036
Of course, your brother
didn't set the bar very high.

10:59.208 --> 11:01.506
Hear, hea- Wait a minute.

11:02.945 --> 11:04.640
Charlie, do you wanna say anything?

11:05.648 --> 11:07.411
Uh, all right.

11:10.119 --> 11:12.587
Alan, you're my little brother.

11:13.356 --> 11:15.688
And I know over the years,
I've tormented you...

11:15.858 --> 11:17.723
...I've embarrassed you in public...

11:17.893 --> 11:20.953
...I've tied you to street lights,
car bumpers...

11:21.130 --> 11:22.859
...the occasional angry animal.

11:24.700 --> 11:26.099
Oh, remember that Fourth of July...

11:26.268 --> 11:28.668
...when I used your ass
as a launch pad for my bottle rockets?

11:30.606 --> 11:33.837
Anyway, I guess
what I'm trying to say is...

11:34.009 --> 11:35.533
...thanks for the memories.

11:39.815 --> 11:41.248
That-? That's it?

11:41.417 --> 11:43.009
That's all you have to say?

11:43.586 --> 11:45.713
I suppose I could talk about
his bed-wetting.

11:49.058 --> 11:51.526
- You people are horrible.
- No, honey, it's okay.

11:51.694 --> 11:53.525
- It's okay.
- No, no, no, it's not okay.

11:53.696 --> 11:55.254
You should be ashamed of yourselves.

11:55.431 --> 11:58.491
This is a warm and wonderful human being
and he deserves more...

11:58.667 --> 12:00.328
...especially from his family.

12:00.503 --> 12:02.528
I don't know
why you guys showed up tonight.

12:02.705 --> 12:05.731
Well, I can't speak for anybody else,
but I'm getting overtime.

12:08.310 --> 12:11.074
- Come on, Alan. We're leaving.
- Really? Before the cake?

12:11.247 --> 12:13.215
You don't need people
who don't appreciate you.

12:13.382 --> 12:16.545
Uh, well, no, but I do kind of need
Charlie's house.

12:16.852 --> 12:20.117
No, you don't. You'll come live with me
and Mom. Right, Mom?

12:20.289 --> 12:23.725
You know, I did spend a summer
in Yosemite doing shrooms...

12:23.893 --> 12:27.989
...so maybe I wasn't
an official forest ranger.

12:28.898 --> 12:30.593
Let's go. Mom, we're leaving.

12:30.766 --> 12:32.324
Okay.

12:32.501 --> 12:34.901
I'm sorry.
This is the best bread I ever had.

12:40.676 --> 12:43.167
Who likes magic?

12:45.848 --> 12:47.440
I shaved for this?

13:11.774 --> 13:14.004
- Berta?
- Who's asking?

13:15.511 --> 13:18.378
- What's wrong?
- Too much celebrating last night.

13:19.281 --> 13:21.374
I didn't notice you drinking
at Alan's party.

13:21.550 --> 13:23.381
No, afterward.

13:23.552 --> 13:26.112
With the magician at his place.

13:28.023 --> 13:31.720
- You went back to his place?
- Well, technically his van.

13:33.696 --> 13:35.163
Why didn't you just stay home?

13:35.331 --> 13:37.959
If I stay home, you don't pay me.

13:38.901 --> 13:41.893
So you just came in
to lie on my couch?

13:42.071 --> 13:44.130
Tough times, Charlie.

13:44.306 --> 13:47.002
Some people are living in their vans.

13:49.178 --> 13:51.840
Oh, make it stop.

13:56.018 --> 13:57.349
Hello.

13:58.053 --> 13:59.645
Hi, Mom.

13:59.855 --> 14:02.653
Alan? No, he didn't come home.

14:03.192 --> 14:07.356
You're right, we were funny.
He just overreacted.

14:08.430 --> 14:11.922
I'm sure he'll come back eventually.
He always does.

14:13.068 --> 14:15.298
You should've named him Herpes.

14:20.976 --> 14:23.843
Yeah, I wish I'd thought of it
last night too.

14:25.981 --> 14:27.778
Talk to you later.

14:28.584 --> 14:30.051
So, what are we gonna do today?

14:31.253 --> 14:34.279
- Aren't you gonna ask about your dad?
- What about him?

14:34.990 --> 14:37.754
Were we not at the same party
last night?

14:38.093 --> 14:42.029
Did you not notice when you finally came
out of the toilet that your father was gone?

14:43.399 --> 14:45.765
You know, now that you mention it...

14:48.537 --> 14:50.937
Herpes Junior.

14:57.680 --> 14:59.739
Oh, look who's back.

14:59.915 --> 15:02.247
I'm not back.
Just came to get my stuff.

15:02.418 --> 15:04.147
You're really gonna milk this, huh?

15:04.320 --> 15:06.481
I'm not milking anything.
There is no milk.

15:06.655 --> 15:08.555
I'm moving in with Melissa
and her mother.

15:08.724 --> 15:10.851
Sounds like milk to me.

15:12.127 --> 15:14.254
I need to be someplace where
I'm appreciated...

15:14.430 --> 15:16.489
...someplace where I, I'm nurtured
and loved.

15:23.639 --> 15:25.664
You're not taking me seriously, are you?

15:25.841 --> 15:28.469
Oh, come on, Alan.
You ain't going anywhere.

15:28.644 --> 15:32.671
You know it, I know it, the seagulls out
there crapping on my deck know it.

15:35.284 --> 15:37.616
"You think he'll be back?"

15:39.788 --> 15:41.449
"Oh, yeah."

15:45.861 --> 15:48.261
No, no. This is it.

15:48.430 --> 15:50.193
This is where I cut the cord.

15:52.968 --> 15:54.526
Oh, man.

15:54.703 --> 15:58.230
I think David Copperfield
slipped me a roofie.

16:01.276 --> 16:03.938
I really appreciate
you taking me in like this.

16:04.113 --> 16:06.445
We love you, Alan. We want you here.

16:06.615 --> 16:09.550
You're a good man
and you have a beautiful soul.

16:10.352 --> 16:14.015
It is beautiful, isn't it?
God forbid my family should notice.

16:14.189 --> 16:15.520
Damn, I knew I'd forget something.

16:15.691 --> 16:18.125
- What'd you forget?
- My son.

16:19.762 --> 16:23.220
Well, that's no problem. We'll just move
Mom's hydroponic equipment...

16:23.399 --> 16:25.765
...out of the garage
and make a bedroom for him.

16:25.934 --> 16:29.233
- Hydroponic equipment?
- Uh, I'm a bit of a horticulturist.

16:29.538 --> 16:31.472
A little herb garden.

16:32.241 --> 16:36.541
Ah, okay. Well, uh, just a heads-up,
I love my son and everything...

16:36.712 --> 16:39.681
...but he hasn't quite gotten
to beautiful soul yet.

16:39.848 --> 16:41.816
He's more methane cloud.

16:42.151 --> 16:44.085
He's still one of God's flowers.

16:44.253 --> 16:47.518
All he needs is a little love,
ultraviolet light, potassium...

16:47.690 --> 16:50.022
...and he'll grow into some
righteous chronic.

17:05.007 --> 17:06.167
Quitting time.

17:20.556 --> 17:22.922
- What are you doing here?
- Watching TV.

17:23.826 --> 17:26.021
- Why didn't you go with your dad?
- Dad was here?

17:27.896 --> 17:31.696
Yeah, he came by to get his stuff
and I figured that included you.

17:31.867 --> 17:34.563
I'm not stuff, Uncle Charlie.
I'm a human being.

17:34.737 --> 17:36.136
Don't flatter yourself.

17:38.941 --> 17:41.068
And turn off the TV.
I'm taking you back to your mom's.

17:41.243 --> 17:42.801
Mom and Herb are in Mexico.

17:43.145 --> 17:44.942
- For how long?
- I don't know.

17:47.116 --> 17:49.550
Turn off the TV.
I'm taking you to Mexico.

17:50.552 --> 17:51.644
Can I drive?

17:56.325 --> 17:59.624
- You all comfy, cozy?
- Uh-huh.

17:59.795 --> 18:02.628
- Mom made you some hot chocolate.
- Oh, oh, thank you.

18:02.798 --> 18:06.063
Oh, and it's got those little marshmallows.
I love those.

18:06.368 --> 18:09.496
Good. I'm going to the market.
What would you like for dinner?

18:09.671 --> 18:11.832
Oh, gosh, I don't know.
What do you want?

18:12.541 --> 18:14.975
I want to please you.

18:18.113 --> 18:19.774
Really?

18:20.449 --> 18:23.179
No one's ever said that to me before.

18:24.186 --> 18:26.154
- Get used to it.
- Heh.

18:26.421 --> 18:28.116
I'll try.

18:28.757 --> 18:30.315
Now, what can I get for you?

18:30.492 --> 18:34.428
Um, well, you know the macaroni
that's shaped like little wagon wheels?

18:34.596 --> 18:37.997
- I do.
- I like that with melted cheese.

18:38.333 --> 18:39.357
- You got it.
- Heh.

18:41.804 --> 18:44.466
Oh, uh, and maybe a couple
of those bottled wine spritzers?

18:44.640 --> 18:46.164
- Okeydoke.
- Ha, ha.

18:49.845 --> 18:51.972
I'm getting mac and spritzers.

18:52.147 --> 18:55.275
I'm getting mac and spritzers.

18:56.318 --> 18:59.185
Here you go, bright eyes.
I made you some banana bread.

18:59.354 --> 19:00.616
- Oh, really?
- Mm-hm.

19:00.789 --> 19:03.121
Banana bread? Oh, thank you.

19:03.292 --> 19:06.159
Oh, man. Wow, it's still warm.

19:06.328 --> 19:07.625
Hmm, right out of the oven.

19:07.796 --> 19:10.663
Mm, hmm, oh, that's-
That's very unusual.

19:10.833 --> 19:13.700
Uh, I'm tasting bananas and,
uh, what is that, nutmeg?

19:14.102 --> 19:15.569
Nope.

19:17.072 --> 19:18.664
- Mm, good.
- You know what?

19:18.841 --> 19:21.036
You might want to start
with half a piece.

19:29.084 --> 19:30.847
I can't believe it.

19:31.286 --> 19:32.981
Believe what?

19:33.455 --> 19:35.013
I think I miss him.

19:35.190 --> 19:36.782
Miss who?

19:39.795 --> 19:41.558
- Your father.
- Oh.

19:43.198 --> 19:46.497
- What about you?
- What about me what?

19:48.003 --> 19:50.563
- Do you miss him?
- Who?

19:52.574 --> 19:55.941
- Your father.
- Why? Where is he?

20:03.518 --> 20:08.478
Honey, they didn't have any spritzers,
so I got you 7UP and sangria.

20:20.469 --> 20:22.198
Alan?

20:23.171 --> 20:27.039
Oh, hey, baby. Have you tried
your mom's banana bread?

20:41.523 --> 20:44.924
- I'm back.
- I'm shocked.

20:49.731 --> 20:51.289
Hey, Alan?

20:51.566 --> 20:52.863
Yeah?

20:53.201 --> 20:54.327
Happy birthday.

20:55.270 --> 20:56.794
Thank you.

21:00.642 --> 21:03.440
- Told you he'd be back.
- Who?
